==Strategy==
Due to the presence of Razorback, bringing [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] is a must.

Provided you don't intend to rush, begin the stage by playing defensively and using the cash from the initial Doge Darks and Gory Darks to level up your Wallet and save up for expensive units like Uber Rare Cats. Once you have enough money, attack the base with a minimal amount of Cats, so that they will die to Kurosawah and the Razorback when they spawn. Allow Razorback to get somewhat to your base, but not too close because of the Tackeys, then permafreeze Razorback with Bombercats.

Send out only a minimal amount of attackers to take care of the peons, but not enough to kill Razorback before the next one spawns. Killing Razorback before the next one spawns will typically result in Kurosawah destroying your stack of Cats, and then any stragglers being ravaged by the next Razorback. Once all 3 Razorbacks have spawned, you can kill them without fear.

After the first time you beat the level, if you are confident in your strategy, bring a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]] and [[Battle Items#Cat Jobs|Cat Jobs]]. With those two items and [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]] thrown in, you can get around '''3 million XP'''.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - An amazing damage dealer with great survivability. Their Talents only make them even better, with Wave Attack allowing them to nuke the Tackeys and Kurosawah from afar, and Slow providing some backup in case your Bombercats get killed. They still get wiped off the earth from Kurosawah though.
*[[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Li'l Gau]], [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]], [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] - All great meatshields for this stage. Gas Mask has a slower recharge and bigger range, so make sure to bring a more spammable meatshield like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]].
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] - If you somehow have them by this point, Jellycat can provide amazing chip damage to Kurosawah and Tackey.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] - Similar to Jellycat, but exchanges ridiculous pierce for sheer damage, along with not dying to a slightly strong gust of air.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Imagawa Yoshimoto (Uber Rare Cat)|Imagawa Yoshimoto]] - A good counter to Tackey, if you can manage to push him into Tackey's blindspot. Guaranteed Weaken makes Tackey less of a threat to your other units.
*[[Seashore Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Seashore Kai]] / [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Keiji]] / [[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]] - Anti-Dark tankers that can stall the enemies whilst dealing some damage, wiping out the weaker pushers.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]] / [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]] / [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]] - Fast, cheap, capable of easily getting into Tackey's blindspot and with short recharge time, they can help a lot for this level. Though be cautious when deploying them, as too much DPS can lead to the Razorbacks dying too fast and getting everyone to Kurosawah's range. They could be helpful for rushing, though that's another matter.
*[[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kuu γ]] - Capable of both taking and dealing a lot of damage at a reasonable range, though be wary of her long attack animation and lengthy attack rate.
*[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Oda Nobunaga]] - Can perma-freeze the nasty pushers like Razorback and tank Tackey hits due to having only 1 knockback.

The vast majority of [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Darks]] help out in here, excluding the ones with knockback ability, as those will push the frontline within Kurosawah's range and kill your whole stack.

